OL,3,GNEWSA'World-beating' study to
OL,4,Ainvestigate social media ban
OL,5,
OL,6,FA "world-beating" multi-generational
OL,7,Fstudy will investigate the effects of
OL,8,Fthe upcoming social media ban for
OL,9,Funder-16s.
OL,11,FParticipants from Bristol-based
OL,12,FChildren of the 90s, which began by
OL,13,Ftracking 14,500 children born between
OL,14,F1991 and 1992, are taking part in a
OL,15,Flarge UK-wide review into the social
OL,16,Fmedia ban.
OL,18,FThe new study will ask children and
OL,19,Fparents about their mental health,
OL,20,Fwellbeing and social media habits
OL,21,Fbefore and after the ban begins.
OL,23,APub: 20-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,342,340,200,160,0,100
